    'ran-063-in-database-encryption-ransomware', 'attacker uses `pgcrypto` / `AES_ENCRYPT` / `ENCRYPTBYKEY` / `DBMS_CRYPTO` to encrypt application columns in-place with a key only they hold. The disk and backup files look normal; file-level EDR sees nothing. Detection: native-crypto function calls + column-type drift to BYTEA/VARBINARY.',
