    'ran-065-federation-dblink-exfiltration', 'attacker creates `postgres_fdw`, dblink, Oracle DBLINK, SQL Server linked server, or MongoDB change-stream pointing at attacker infrastructure. Data ships off-host directly from the DB engine, bypassing host-network monitoring. The PostgreSQL dblink+`COPY FROM` chain is documented as the canonical exfil route (HackTricks, NetSPI, Imperva).',
